[{"id":"rq-predict-sat","itemId":"requantiser","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"Lesson 12.2's <code class=\"nobreak\">requant</code> with S = 2 and the multiplier <code class=\"nobreak\">m</code> set to 4. A finished sum goes in on <code class=\"nobreak\">acc</code> while <code class=\"nobreak\">in_valid</code> is 1, and two rising edges later <code class=\"nobreak\">sat</code> says whether its result was clipped to 255. <code class=\"nobreak\">acc</code> is drawn in hexadecimal. Cycles 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">sat</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p>With <code class=\"nobreak\">m</code> 4 and S 2, a sum is multiplied by 4, 2 is added, and the shift by 2 divides by 4: the result is the sum itself. So <code class=\"nobreak\">sat</code> is 1 for the sums over 255, 100 (256) and 190 (400). Each shows two rising edges after it goes in on <code class=\"nobreak\">acc</code>, one edge after the edge that takes it: 0 for D in cycle 2, 0 for FF (255, the largest that fits) in cycle 3, 1 in cycle 4, 0 for 64 in cycle 5, 1 in cycle 6, and 0 for the 0 in cycle 7.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"rq-sat","source":"hdl/level-12/requant/requant_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"requant_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"]]},{"label":"in_valid","path":"requant_tb.in_valid","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[0.5,"1"],[6.5,"0"]]},{"label":"acc[25:0]","path":"requant_tb.acc","width":26,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"00000000000000000000000000"],[0.5,"00000000000000000000001101"],[1.5,"00000000000000000011111111"],[2.5,"00000000000000000100000000"],[3.5,"00000000000000000001100100"],[4.5,"00000000000000000110010000"],[5.5,"00000000000000000000000000"]]},{"label":"sat","path":"requant_tb.sat","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[4,"1"],[5,"0"],[6,"1"],[7,"0"]],"samples":["0","0","0","0","1","0","1","0"]}]},"answer":"sat","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"rq-predict-round","itemId":"requantiser","role":"core","promptHtml":"Lesson 12.2's <code class=\"nobreak\">requant</code> with S = 2 and the multiplier <code class=\"nobreak\">m</code> set to 7. A finished sum goes in on <code class=\"nobreak\">acc</code> while <code class=\"nobreak\">in_valid</code> is 1, and two rising edges later <code class=\"nobreak\">sat</code> says whether its result was clipped to 255. <code class=\"nobreak\">acc</code> is drawn in hexadecimal. In cycles 0 and 1, <code class=\"nobreak\">sat</code> still shows sums from before: 0. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">sat</code> for every cycle.","explanationHtml":"<p>The result is 7 times the sum, plus 2, shifted right by 2, and <code class=\"nobreak\">sat</code> is 1 when that is over 255. 91 is 145: 1,015 + 2 = 1,017 gives 254, kept. 92 is 146: 1,022 + 2 = 1,024 gives 256, clipped, though without the rounding it would have been 255. 90 is 144: 1,008 + 2 = 1,010 gives 252. 93 is 147: 257, clipped. 64 is 100: 175. Each shows two edges after its sum went in: 1 in cycles 3 and 5 only.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"rq-round","source":"hdl/level-12/requant/requant_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":7,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"requant_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"]]},{"label":"in_valid","path":"requant_tb.in_valid","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[0.5,"1"],[5.5,"0"]]},{"label":"acc[25:0]","path":"requant_tb.acc","width":26,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"00000000000000000000000000"],[0.5,"00000000000000000010010001"],[1.5,"00000000000000000010010010"],[2.5,"00000000000000000010010000"],[3.5,"00000000000000000010010011"],[4.5,"00000000000000000001100100"],[5.5,"00000000000000000000000000"]]},{"label":"sat","path":"requant_tb.sat","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[3,"1"],[4,"0"],[5,"1"],[6,"0"]],"samples":["0","0","0","1","0","1","0"]}]},"answer":"sat"},{"id":"rq-find-bug","itemId":"requantiser","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">requant_bug</code> should clip a result over 255 to 255, as lesson 12.2's <code class=\"nobreak\">requant</code> does. Its testbench fails on the sum 256 with <code class=\"nobreak\">m</code> 4: <code class=\"nobreak\">sat</code> is 1, as it should be, but <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> is 0 instead of 255. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">r[7:0]</code> keeps only the low 8 bits of the result. 256 is 1 0000 0000, so its low 8 bits are 0, and 400 would give 144: a value too big for 8 bits wraps round. <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code> must take 255 whenever <code class=\"nobreak\">r</code> is over 255, the same test that <code class=\"nobreak\">sat</code> makes.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-12/requant_bug/requant_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// The 3D decoder's requantiser, in small: it turns a finished sum back","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// into an 8-bit activation for the next layer. ReLU first: a negative","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// sum becomes 0. Then the channel's multiplier m. Then a shift right by","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// S, rounded to the nearest whole number by adding half of 2**S first.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// Last, a result over 255, the largest 8-bit value, is clipped to 255","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// rather than wrapping round. Two stages: the product at one rising","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// edge, the result at the next.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"requant_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"#","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"parameter","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"int","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" S ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"2","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"                    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// the layer's shift","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":") (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"               clk,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"               in_valid,   ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// acc is a finished sum","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"signed","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"25","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] acc,        ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// the sum: 25 bits and a sign","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"        [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"15","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] m,          ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// the channel's multiplier","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"               out_valid,  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// q is a new activation","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"        [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"7","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"]  q,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"               sat         ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// q was clipped to 255","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"24","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] a;                        ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// after ReLU","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"40","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] prod;                     ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// a * m, one edge later","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"        v1;                       ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// in_valid, one edge later","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"40","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] r;                        ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// rounded and shifted","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" a ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" acc[","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"25","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"?","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"25'd0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" acc[","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"24","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"];","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" r ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" (prod ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"+","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"41'd1","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<<","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" (S ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"-","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"1","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"))) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":">>","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" S;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_ff","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"@","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"(","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"posedge","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" clk) ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"    prod      ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" a ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"*","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" m;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    v1        ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" in_valid;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    out_valid ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" v1;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    sat       ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" (r ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":">","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"41'd255","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    q         ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"<=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" r[","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"7","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"];","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]],"bugLine":32,"fixLine":"q         <= (r > 41'd255) ? 8'd255 : r[7:0];"},{"id":"rq-fill-round","itemId":"requantiser","role":"core","promptHtml":"In lesson 12.2's <code class=\"nobreak\">requant</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">r</code> must be <code class=\"nobreak\">prod</code> divided by 2 to the power S, rounded to the nearest whole number rather than down. Fill in what is added to <code class=\"nobreak\">prod</code> before the shift.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>(41'd1 &lt;&lt; (S - 1))</code>: 2 to the power S − 1, half the divisor. Adding half before dividing rounds to the nearest: with S = 2, 41 / 4 is 10.25, and (41 + 2) / 4 gives 10; 42 / 4 is 10.5, and (42 + 2) / 4 gives 11. Without it, the shift rounds every result down.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-12/requant/requant.sv","firstLine":19,"totalLines":34,"before":["  logic [24:0] a;                        // after ReLU","  logic [40:0] prod;                     // a * m, one edge later","  logic        v1;                       // in_valid, one edge later","  logic [40:0] r;                        // rounded and shifted","","  assign a = acc[25] ? 25'd0 : acc[24:0];"],"blankLine":{"left":"  assign r = (prod + ","right":") >> S;"},"after":[],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"24","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] a;                        ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// after ReLU","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"40","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] prod;                     ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// a * m, one edge later","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"        v1;                       ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// in_valid, one edge later","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"40","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] r;                        ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// rounded and shifted","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" a ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" acc[","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"25","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"?","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"25'd0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" acc[","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"24","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"];","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" r ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" (prod ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"+","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":") ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":">>","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" S;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]},"after":[]},"accept":["(41'd1 << (S - 1))","(1 << (S - 1))","(41'd1 << S - 1)","(1 << S - 1)","2 ** (S - 1)","(2 ** (S - 1))"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"Half of 2 to the power S"},{"id":"rq-order-steps","itemId":"requantiser","role":"core","promptHtml":"Put in order what happens, in the engine of one of the 3D decoder's two middle layers, on the way to one output channel's activation at one voxel.","explanationHtml":"<p>A lane multiplies eight activations by their weights and adds the eight products, and that total joins the running sum; this repeats until the sum has every product. Only the finished sum goes to the requantiser, which turns one channel a cycle into an activation while the engine works on its next sums. Requantising a part sum would round and clip it too early, and ReLU would throw away negative parts that later products could outweigh.</p>","type":"order","steps":["Eight activations are multiplied by their eight 4-bit weights.","The eight products are added together.","That total is added to the channel's running sum.","Once the sum has every product, it goes to the requantiser.","The requantiser turns the sum into an 8-bit activation.","The activation is written to the layer's output, for the next engine."],"shuffled":[0,1,5,3,2,4]},{"id":"rq-report-dsp","itemId":"requantiser","role":"core","promptHtml":"Lesson 12.2's <code class=\"nobreak\">requant</code> has 52 bits of registers in its code: <code class=\"nobreak\">prod</code>, 41 bits, <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code>, 8 bits, and <code class=\"nobreak\">sat</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">v1</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">out_valid</code>, 1 bit each. Vivado used one DSP48E1 for its multiply. Below is the Slice Logic table of its Utilization report.","explanationHtml":"<p>Read the Register as Flip Flop row: 11, for <code class=\"nobreak\">q</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">sat</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">v1</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">out_valid</code>. <code class=\"nobreak\">prod</code>'s register comes straight after the multiplier, where the DSP48E1 has registers of its own (lesson 6.3), so its 41 bits are inside the block. In the decoder's first board build, each of its three hidden requantisers was one DSP block too.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/requant/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":32,"excerpt":["+-------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+","|        Site Type        | Used | Fixed | Prohibited | Available | Util% |","+-------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+","| Slice LUTs              |   27 |     0 |          0 |     63400 |  0.04 |","|   LUT as Logic          |   27 |     0 |          0 |     63400 |  0.04 |","|   LUT as Memory         |    0 |     0 |          0 |     19000 |  0.00 |","| Slice Registers         |   11 |     0 |          0 |    126800 | <0.01 |","|   Register as Flip Flop |   11 |     0 |          0 |    126800 | <0.01 |","|   Register as Latch     |    0 |     0 |          0 |    126800 |  0.00 |","| F7 Muxes                |    0 |     0 |          0 |     31700 |  0.00 |","| F8 Muxes                |    0 |     0 |          0 |     15850 |  0.00 |","| Unique Control Sets     |    2 |       |          0 |     15850 |  0.01 |","+-------------------------+------+-------+------------+-----------+-------+"],"ask":"How many flip-flops does requant use?","answer":"11","numeric":true}]